  "notes": "\"The rhythmically busiest of the three\", and the model says that in the kick: `densityPerBar` [6, 8] at `syncopation` 0.74 is the busiest kick in this batch by a clear margin, against Jeezy's [2, 3] at 0.18. The rest follows the darker half of the research paragraph. \"Often harmonic-minor with an augmented-2nd colour\" leads the scale weights — the only entry in the batch where `harmonic_minor` outranks everything — and the palette is choir and detuned brass rather than bell. \"Hard-attack distorted 808, pitch movement in 4ths/5ths, glides on the last 16th of the bar\" is `distortion: heavy` with a `P4`/`P5` interval set and `slidePositions` reduced to `phrase_end`, which is where the last 16th of a bar lands. \"Melody often just a rhythmic ostinato\" over a \"wide register spread\" and a \"low pitch count\" is `motifPitchCount` 4 across a 30-semitone melodic register with `contour.riff` at 0.82. The \"mid-song beat switch used more often than his peers\" is `transitions.switchUpProb` 0.32, the highest here. ⚠ **The roll frequency is capped at 0.20 by this batch's authoring band**, and the research asks for \"fast 32nd/64th rolls\": the vocabulary is fixed to 16ths in this band, so the aggression is carried by the roll's ramp (the widest velocity span in the batch, [45, 103]) and by `gapProb` 0.08 rather than by finer subdivisions. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` — the research rates the entry high-medium with no per-session sourcing. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the reverse-crash as a perc lane, and the family weights. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
